&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Broke out the sword from the amazing Bloody Glorious Hawk Boy model to use as a spiritual weapon for a DND Cleric character and got a lot of requests to post the STL. Recommend printing on a resin printer. If you have a really well dialed in FDM printer you can try printing the file as it&amp;#39;s imported with supports to have the best chance of getting the flames to come out. Might not be a bad idea to scale up to 110 or 120% for FDM to give the fine details a better chance.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
